  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.35",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $G$ be a finite group, $w$ a multilinear commutator group-word, and $p$ a prime. Suppose that $p$ divides the order $|xy|$ whenever $x$ is a $w$-value of $p'$-order in $G$ and $y$ is a $w$-value in $G$ of order divisible by $p$. Is it true that then the verbal subgroup $w(G)$ must be $p$-nilpotent?",
